// Auto-generated Make.com knowledge pack for Wire (from research workflow).
module.exports = "\n# Make.com Knowledge Pack (for Wire)\n\nMake.com (formerly Integromat) is a visual no-/low-code automation platform. You build **scenarios** \u2014 directed graphs of **modules** \u2014 that move and transform data between apps. This pack teaches the mental model, the flow-control toolkit, and the exact **blueprint JSON** you emit to BUILD scenarios via the API, plus how to STUDY existing ones. Verified against developers.make.com and the official integromat/make-skills repo (Aug 2026).\n\n## 1. Core concepts\n- **Scenario**: one automation/workflow. It has a **flow** (ordered modules), a **schedule**, and settings. Its live URL is `https://<zone>/<teamId>/scenarios/<scenarioId>`.\n- **Module**: one step doing one task. Types: **Trigger** (polling \u2014 \"Watch new rows\", runs on a schedule and remembers the last item processed), **Instant trigger** (webhook \u2014 fires the instant data arrives), **Action** (single operation \u2192 single response, e.g. create/get/update/delete a record), **Search** (returns many matching items \u2192 many bundles), plus **Universal/HTTP** (arbitrary API calls) and **Responder** (returns data to a webhook caller). **Every scenario begins with exactly one trigger.**\n- **Bundle**: one packet of data flowing between modules. A module runs once per bundle. A search/iterator emits many bundles.\n- **Connection**: stored, reusable authentication to an app (OAuth/API key). In blueprints a module references it by ID via `__IMTCONN__`.\n- **Operation / Credit**: an **operation** = one module run processing one bundle (5 emails = 5 ops). Since Nov 2025 billing is in **credits**: non-AI modules \u2248 1 credit/op; AI modules and multi-bundle modules cost more. **Data transfer** (bytes moved) is metered alongside. Optimize by filtering early, batching, aggregating, and running less often.\n- **Apps library**: 3,000+ integrations (OpenAI, Anthropic Claude, Google Gemini/Sheets/Calendar, Airtable, HubSpot, monday.com, Slack, Gmail, Notion, \u2026). Built-in/generic apps: **HTTP** (call any REST API), **Webhooks** (receive inbound HTTP \u2192 instant trigger; also respond), **JSON** (parse/create), and **Flow Control & Tools** (routers, iterators, aggregators, utilities).\n\n## 2. Flow control\n- **Router** (`builtin:BasicRouter`): duplicates the incoming bundle down multiple **routes**; every matching route runs (NOT mutually exclusive, routes cannot merge back). Gate each route with a **filter** on its first module. Supports a **fallback** route for bundles matching no other route.\n- **Filter**: a gate between two modules (or on a route). Only bundles meeting conditions pass. Conditions combine as OR (outer) of AND (inner).\n- **Iterator** (`builtin:BasicFeeder`): splits one bundle containing an array into one bundle per element, processed sequentially.\n- **Aggregator**: inverse of iterator \u2014 collects many bundles into one. Variants: **Array** (`builtin:BasicAggregator`), **Text** (`util:TextAggregator`, concatenate with a separator), Numeric (sum/avg/count/min/max), Table. Each aggregator names a **Source Module** (the `feeder` id) where the loop began. When a Filter sits between Iterator and Aggregator, point the aggregator's feeder at the **Iterator**, not the Filter.\n- **If-Else** (`builtin:BasicIfElse`, convergent): mutually exclusive branches; only the first matching branch runs, then a separate `builtin:BasicMerge` module rejoins them. (Contrast with routers, which fan out.)\n\n## 3. Data stores\nMake's built-in key-value database that persists data **between runs** without an external DB. Each store follows a data structure; every record has a unique **Key** (you supply one or Make generates a UUID) plus fields. Modules: Add/Replace, Get, Update, Search, Delete. Use for deduplication, caching state, and passing data between scenarios (e.g. store a `last_sync` timestamp for incremental syncs).\n\n## 4. Functions (mapping-time transforms)\nUppercase in docs but **case-insensitive**; parameters separated by **semicolons** (not commas); text literals in double quotes; nestable; usable in any mappable field. Categories: General/logic (`if`, `ifempty`, `switch`, `get`, `length`), Math (`sum`, `average`, `ceil`, `floor`, `round`, `min`, `max`), Text (`upper`, `lower`, `trim`, `replace`, `substring`, `split`, `contains`), Date (`now`, `formatDate`, `parseDate`, `addDays`, `addMinutes`; Moment.js tokens `YYYY MM DD HH mm`), Array (`map`, `join`, `merge`, `sort`, `distinct`, `slice`, `add`). Examples: `formatDate(now; \"YYYY-MM-DD\")`, `map(1.items; \"email\")`, `if(1.status = \"paid\"; \"Thanks!\"; \"Pending\")`, `split(1.\\`1\\`; space)`.\n\n## 5. Error handling\nAttach a handler to a fragile module; it becomes the last module on that module's error route. Five directives + Retry:\n- **Ignore**: skip the failed bundle, continue others (run = Success).\n- **Resume**: substitute a fallback output for the failed module so downstream runs normally (Success).\n- **Commit**: stop but keep already-committed side effects (Success).\n- **Rollback** (default when no handler): stop and revert transactions (run = Error).\n- **Break**: park the failed bundle in **Incomplete Executions** for later manual/auto retry (Warning); remaining bundles continue.\n- **Retry**: re-attempt the module N times.\n\nError types drive automatic reactions: **RateLimitError** (scenario suspended ~20 min then resumed, not counted), **ConnectionError**/**ModuleTimeoutError** (backoff + retry), **DataError/DuplicateDataError** (stored for repair if enabled), config/token errors (deactivate + notify). **\"Store incomplete executions\" is OFF by default** \u2014 enable it in scenario settings; Make auto-retries RateLimit/Connection/ModuleTimeout and Break/Retry-origin items with **exponential backoff**. Scenarios auto-deactivate after a configurable number of **consecutive errors** (warnings don't count).\n\n## 6. Scheduling\nAn activated scenario's clock: **Immediately** (webhook/instant triggers), **At regular intervals** (minutes; polling default 15 min), Once, Every day, Days of week, Days of month, specified dates, advanced (start/end + restrictions), and **On demand** (only via manual run or API). Instant webhooks process in **parallel** as requests arrive. A webhook on a **schedule** instead queues requests and processes up to **\"Maximum number of results\"** (default 2) per run; requests also queue while a scenario is OFF. Minimum interval: **15 min (Free), 1 min (paid)**; max execution: **5 min (Free), 40 min (paid)**.\n\n## 7. Blueprint JSON format (what you emit to BUILD)\nA blueprint has exactly three top-level keys: **`name`** (string), **`flow`** (array of modules), **`metadata`** (object, REQUIRED even if you only care about flow).\n\nEach module object:\n- `id` \u2014 unique positive integer, sequential from 1.\n- `module` \u2014 `namespace:ModuleName` (e.g. `gateway:CustomWebHook`, `json:ParseJSON`, `google-sheets:addRow`, `builtin:BasicRouter`, `email:ActionSendEmail`, `http:ActionSendData`).\n- `version` \u2014 integer matching the app/module version.\n- `parameters` \u2014 fixed config + IDs: connection via `__IMTCONN__`, webhook via `__IMTHOOK__`, aggregator/iterator source via `feeder`.\n- `mapper` \u2014 dynamic per-run values using `{{id.field}}` references.\n- `metadata.designer` \u2014 `{x, y, name}` layout (x usually +300 per module).\n- `filter` \u2014 gate object or `null`.\n- `routes` \u2014 (routers only) top-level array of `{flow:[...]}`.\n- `onerror` \u2014 nested array of directive modules.\n\n**Mapping syntax**: `{{1.email}}` (field of module 1); `` {{1.`0`}} `` (spreadsheet column by index, backticks); `{{1.choices[].message.content}}` (iterate array field); `{{1.__IMTLENGTH__}}` (bundle count); functions wrap refs: `{{formatDate(now; \"YYYY-MM-DD\")}}`, `{{lower(1.name)}}`. Keep **fixed** values in `parameters`, **dynamic** values in `mapper`.\n\n**Router**: `{\"id\":2,\"module\":\"builtin:BasicRouter\",\"version\":1,\"routes\":[{\"flow\":[{...}]},{\"flow\":[{...}]}]}`; per-branch `filter` on the first module of each route's flow.\n\n**Iterator + Aggregator**:\n```\n{\"id\":2,\"module\":\"builtin:BasicFeeder\",\"version\":1,\"mapper\":{\"array\":\"{{1.items}}\"}}\n{\"id\":3,\"module\":\"builtin:BasicAggregator\",\"version\":1,\"parameters\":{\"feeder\":2},\"mapper\":{\"properties\":{\"email\":\"{{2.value}}\"}}}\n{\"id\":10,\"module\":\"util:TextAggregator\",\"version\":1,\"parameters\":{\"feeder\":8,\"rowSeparator\":\"\\n\"},\"mapper\":{\"value\":\"{{8.description}}\"}}\n```\n\n**Filter object**:\n```\n\"filter\":{\"name\":\"Only active high-priority\",\n  \"conditions\":[[{\"a\":\"{{1.status}}\",\"b\":\"ACTIVE\",\"o\":\"text:equal:ci\"},\n                 {\"a\":\"{{1.priority}}\",\"b\":\"high\",\"o\":\"text:equal\"}]]}\n```\n`a`=left, `b`=right (omit for `exist`/`notexist`), `o`=operator (`text:equal`, `text:equal:ci`, `text:contain`, `number:greater`, `date:before`, `exist`, `notexist`, \u2026). Outer array = OR groups, inner = AND.\n\n**onerror** (nested in a module): `\"onerror\":[{\"id\":99,\"module\":\"builtin:Resume\",\"version\":1,\"mapper\":{\"output\":\"fallback\"}}]`. Directives: `builtin:Resume`, `builtin:Commit`, `builtin:Rollback`, `builtin:Ignore`, `builtin:Break`.\n\n**If-Else (convergent)**: a `builtin:BasicIfElse` module whose `branches` array holds objects of `type:\"condition\"` (with `conditions`) or `type:\"else\"`, each with `merge:true` and its own `flow`, followed in the top-level flow by a `builtin:BasicMerge` module.\n\n**Scenario-level `metadata`** keys: `instant` (bool, true for webhook triggers), `version` (int), `scenario` object `{roundtrips, maxErrors, autoCommit, autoCommitTriggerLast, sequential, confidential, dataloss, dlq, freshVariables}`, `designer:{orphans:[]}`, `zone` (e.g. `\"eu2.make.com\"`).\n\n## 8. How to BUILD via API\n`POST /scenarios` with body `{ teamId (int), blueprint (STRING), scheduling (STRING), folderId?, description?, basedon?, metadata? }`. Critical: **`blueprint` and `scheduling` are JSON-serialized STRINGS, not nested objects** (\"to save resources, the blueprint is sent as a string\"). `scheduling` string examples: `{\"type\":\"immediately\"}` (webhook/instant), `{\"type\":\"indefinitely\",\"interval\":900}` (interval in **seconds**), `{\"type\":\"once\"}`, on-demand. After create, use `POST /scenarios/{id}/start` to activate, `POST /scenarios/{id}/run` for a one-off (returns `{\"executionId\":\"...\"}`; `responsive:true` waits \u226440s; `callbackUrl` gets a POST on finish). Distinguish `/run` (one execution) from `/start`|`/stop` (toggle active state). Update with `PATCH /scenarios/{id}` (only supplied fields change).\n\n## 9. How to STUDY an existing scenario\n`GET /scenarios/{id}/blueprint` returns `{code, response:{blueprint:{flow, name, metadata, scheduling, idSequence, ...}}}`. Query `draft=true|false` for draft vs live and `blueprintId` for a specific version; `GET /scenarios/{id}/blueprints` lists versions (only \u226460 days old). **The single most reliable way to get a correct `module` identifier + `version` + parameter/mapper shape is to build once in the UI (or find an existing scenario) and read its blueprint** \u2014 module names and versions vary per app (e.g. Make's generic email app is `email:ActionSendEmail`; the Gmail app namespace is `google-email`, so confirm before assuming `gmail:...`).\n\n## 10. Key gotchas\n1. Target the **correct zone host** \u2014 an eu1 token fails against us1.\n2. Paths are **case-sensitive**; multi-word resources use **hyphens** (`data-stores`).\n3. `blueprint` + `scheduling` \u2192 **stringified JSON** on create.\n4. `metadata` is **required** on the blueprint.\n5. Team-scoped list endpoints need `teamId` (scenarios also accept `organizationId`); `teams` needs `organizationId`; `organizations` needs neither.\n6. Pagination `pg[limit] pg[offset] pg[sortBy] pg[sortDir]` and field selection `cols[]`; **percent-encode brackets** (`pg%5BsortDir%5D=asc`).\n7. Token must carry the exact **scope** (e.g. `scenarios:run` for `/run`).\n8. Module `id`s unique + sequential; `version` must match the app.\n9. `parameters` (fixed/ids) vs `mapper` (dynamic `{{}}`) are separate objects.\n10. Make API org rate limits: Core 60 / Pro 120 / Teams 240 / Enterprise 1000 req/min (HTTP 429 on excess; `/run` is exempt). Third-party API limits inside scenarios surface as `RateLimitError`.\n\n\n## Minimal blueprint example (valid JSON to model after)\n{\n  \"name\": \"Webhook to Email\",\n  \"flow\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 1,\n      \"module\": \"gateway:CustomWebHook\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"parameters\": { \"__IMTHOOK__\": 99251 },\n      \"mapper\": {},\n      \"metadata\": { \"designer\": { \"x\": 0, \"y\": 0, \"name\": \"Webhook\" } }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 2,\n      \"module\": \"email:ActionSendEmail\",\n      \"version\": 7,\n      \"parameters\": { \"__IMTCONN__\": 12345 },\n      \"mapper\": {\n        \"to\": [\"{{1.email}}\"],\n        \"subject\": \"Hello {{1.name}}\",\n        \"contentType\": \"text\",\n        \"html\": \"Body: {{1.message}}\"\n      },\n      \"filter\": null,\n      \"metadata\": { \"designer\": { \"x\": 300, \"y\": 0, \"name\": \"Send Email\" } }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"instant\": true,\n    \"version\": 1,\n    \"scenario\": {\n      \"roundtrips\": 1,\n      \"maxErrors\": 3,\n      \"autoCommit\": true,\n      \"autoCommitTriggerLast\": true,\n      \"sequential\": false,\n      \"confidential\": false,\n      \"dataloss\": false,\n      \"dlq\": false,\n      \"freshVariables\": false\n    },\n    \"designer\": { \"orphans\": [] },\n    \"zone\": \"eu2.make.com\"\n  }\n}";
